  <Docs>
    <summary>
            Exposes the cross-platform modal navigation state that a <see cref="T:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatform" />
            needs in order to present and dismiss modal pages.
            </summary>
    <remarks>
      <para>
            The framework implements this interface and supplies an instance to
            <see cref="M:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatformFactory.CreateModalNavigationPlatform(Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationHost)" />.
            One host exists per <see cref="P:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationHost.Window" />, so an implementation must never be shared
            between windows.
            </para>
      <para>
            The framework owns the cross-platform modal stack, the page lifecycle events
            (<c>Appearing</c>/<c>Disappearing</c>, <c>NavigatedTo</c>/<c>NavigatedFrom</c>), the
            <see cref="E:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Window.ModalPushing" />/<see cref="E:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Window.ModalPopped" /> events and the
            reconciliation loop that keeps the platform stack in sync with the requested stack. A platform
            implementation is only responsible for the visual presentation of a single push or pop.
            </para>
      <para>
            Every member except <see cref="M:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationHost.RequestSync" /> must be read on the UI thread.
            </para>
    </remarks>
  </Docs>
