      <Docs>
        <summary>
            Gets a value indicating whether the framework side of the window is ready for modal
            presentation: the window and its page both have handlers.
            </summary>
        <value>To be added.</value>
        <remarks>
          <para>
            This intentionally does <b>not</b> include
            <see cref="P:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatform.IsReady" />. Implementations are expected to combine it
            with their own conditions, for example
            <c>public bool IsReady =&gt; _host.IsWindowReady &amp;&amp; _nativeWindowIsRealized;</c>.
            Because the framework folds <see cref="P:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatform.IsReady" /> into its own
            overall readiness separately, a host property that already included it would recurse into an
            uncatchable <see cref="T:System.StackOverflowException" />.
            </para>
          <para>
            Consulting this from <see cref="P:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatform.IsReady" /> is optional. The framework
            never calls <see cref="M:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatform.PushModalAsync(Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Page,System.Boolean)" /> or
            <see cref="M:Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Platform.IModalNavigationPlatform.PopModalAsync(Microsoft.Maui.Controls.Page,System.Boolean)" /> unless this is already
            <see langword="true" />.
            </para>
        </remarks>
      </Docs>
    </Member>
